ile alongside the PDF\\n\\n- Function parse_items_from_response(response: dict) -> list[dict] that:\\n  - First checks if 'extracted_data' has items (from Extract step)\\n  - If not, looks for Table elements with text_as_html and parses the HTML tables\\n  - If no structured tables, falls back to parsing the text content\\n  - Returns list of {\\\"item_name_raw\\\": str, \\\"source_page\\\": int|None}\\n\\n- Function extract_items_from_pdf(filepath: Path, api_key: str, base_url: str = 'https://transform.unstructured.io') -> list[dict] that:\\n  - Calls extract_from_pdf to get the response\\n  - Then calls parse_items_from_response\\n  - Adds source_file to each item\\n  - Returns the final list\\n\\nFor the HTML table parsing, use a simple approach:\\n- Parse the text_as_html field from Table elements\\n- Find the column that contains drug names (usually the second column after a code column, or the column with Arabic text)\\n- Extract each row's drug name cell\\n\\nIMPORTANT: The Unstructured API uses:\\n- POST to https://transform.unstructured.io/api/v2/parse\\n- Header: unstructured-api-key\\n- Form data: profile=best, output=elements  \\n- File upload: input=(filename, content, 'application/pdf')\\n- Response may be immediate (200) or async (202 with Location header for polling)\\n- Poll URL returns job status, wait for status='completed'\\n\\n## 9. src/extract/file_handler.py\\nUnified file handler that detects file typ\n---\nThe checkpoint summary has been truncated due to hitting max length. Please see the conversation log file for the full conversation.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
