{"step_index":656,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T00:14:56Z","thinking":"**Reviewing Immediate UI Load**\n\nI'm currently focused on the instant appearance of the confirmation modal upon application startup, which seems to be a UI layering issue, per the image and user's statement. This modal, as the user mentioned, is blocking interaction. My primary concern is the timing of the display relative to the overall UI load. I'm investigating how this modal's rendering is triggered and if there's a way to delay its activation until after other interface elements are ready.\n\n\n**Debugging Modal Visibility**\n\nMy current troubleshooting focuses on the immediate modal display at application launch. I believe a conflict between the inline style `display: flex;` and the `.hidden` class might be causing the issue. I am reviewing the CSS to confirm that the `.hidden` class's `display: none !important;` rule is properly overriding any inline styles. Additionally, I've noted that the buttons lack initial `onclick` handlers, contributing to their non-responsiveness. I'm investigating how the modal is shown.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python -c \\\"import re; lines=open('d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/desktop_app/templates/index.html', encoding='utf-8').readlines(); print(''.join(lines[705:750]))\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"500","toolAction":"\"Check modal HTML\"","toolSummary":"\"Check modal HTML\""}}]}
